  "live_records": {
    "q-164419": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164419",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(x-1)^{2}=3y?$",
      "worked_solution": "The full expression describing all points on our parabolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}=3y,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:(x-1)^{2}=3y\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is an upward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(1,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
