    "q-164418": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164418",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $(x-3)^{2}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{8}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{8}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x-3)^{2}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{8}=1\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(3,-6).$",
