    "q-164423": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164423",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "The full expression describing all points on our elliptic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1\\}\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=1\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse centered at $(-3,0)$ with semi-axes of lengths $1$ and $5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
