    "q-164415": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164415",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic cylinder $2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2}=10$ and the plane $z=5$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=5,$ we substitute $z=5$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
