    "q-164397": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164397",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-4)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =1 \\\\ 8-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =7 \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =49 \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ y & =-1\\pm 7 \\\\ y & =-8,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=-8$ and $y=6$ in the $yz$-plane.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-164397-a",
