    "q-164404": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164404",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(y-4)^{2}=z+1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =0+1 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =1 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ y & =4\\pm 1 \\\\ y & =3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=3$ and $y=5$ in the $xy$-plane.",
