      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(0)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =8 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ x & =1\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines in the $xz$-plane.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
